# SonoJS blocks preview — login pattern

Canonical surface: `/blocks/authentication/login` (`login-01` …). **Same stage / card rule everywhere** — docs `BlockExample`, `/view/[name]` embeds, and installable demos.

## Stage vs card

| Layer | Token | Role |
|---|---|---|
| Desktop preview stage | `bg-canvas` (same as `--background`) | Soft gray page behind the demo |
| Tablet/mobile letterbox | `bg-transparency` | Checkerboard void around the shrunk viewport — reads as transparent/empty, not solid white or muted fill |
| Device bezel | none | No extra border/shadow around the phone — only the block’s own `bg-card` |
| Elevated UI card | `bg-card` + `border-border/70` + `shadow-soft` + `rounded-[12px]` | The floating form / panel |

**Never** paint the `BlockExample` stage (or device iframe chrome) with `bg-card`. Card-on-card kills `shadow-soft`.

## Docs `BlockExample`

```tsx
// ✅ Card demos (login, tabs, breadcrumbs, …)
<BlockExample name="login-01" usage={…}>
  <div className="flex w-full items-center justify-center bg-canvas px-10 py-10">
    <div className="w-full max-w-md">
      <LoginForm /> {/* itself: bg-card shadow-soft */}
    </div>
  </div>
</BlockExample>

// ✅ Or omit previewClassName (stage defaults to bg-canvas) and wrap the same way.

// ✅ Full-bleed chrome (navbar, sidebar, footer, mega-menu, …)
<BlockExample
  name="navbar-01"
  previewAlign="start"
  previewClassName="bg-canvas p-0"
  …
>

// ❌ Stage same color as the card — shadow disappears
previewClassName="bg-card"
```

## `/view/[name]` embeds

Match the docs shell: `bg-canvas` + padding when the block is a floating card; `bg-canvas` / `bg-background` full-bleed when the block is a page chrome.

## Shadow must not be clipped

`shadow-soft` spreads ~28px down. Desktop `BlockExample` preview must use `overflow-visible` (not `overflow-hidden`) on the stage/chrome so the bottom of the card shadow isn’t cut by the frame. Keep padding (`px-10 py-12`) so the blur has room inside the canvas.

## Checklist

- [ ] Desktop stage is `bg-canvas` (not `bg-card`)
- [ ] Tablet/mobile letterbox is `bg-transparency` (checkerboard void); device has no extra border/shadow
- [ ] Floating panels use `bg-card shadow-soft`
- [ ] Enough padding (`px-10 py-12` or similar) so the soft shadow is visible
- [ ] Desktop preview does not `overflow-hidden` the stage (shadow intact)
- [ ] Tablet/mobile iframe pages use the same canvas shell
